One transaction only: EnclaveHostOwnership(0xbbd885d3).proposeOwner(metal0,
Enclave wallet 0x0b2d) from the registry operator 0xc9d0, exactly tx 1 of the
public plan metal0-enrollment-unsigned-20261023.json (sha256 9f6eba17).
Two RPCs at one agreed block: ownership code hash and registry; metal0's entry
(active, operator, payout, endpoint); authority zero/zero; the operator's
EXACT EIP-7702 delegation to the reviewed executor runtime; nonce settled;
simulation; gas <= 150000, maxFee <= 0.1 gwei, gas*maxFee + Base L1 upper
bound <= 0.000005 ETH; balance at send.
The key is read only by --send, after fresh checks. The signed bytes are
journaled 0600 and fsynced before broadcast. Resume never signs and re-sends
only the same bytes; a nonce conflict is final. Verification needs agreeing
receipts, 2 confirmations, an exact tx and the pending owner.
Tests: a two-RPC fake chain with a test key, 15/15. All 9 safety mutants fail
the suite. Nothing was signed or sent.
